# Corpus files that test an API the specifications do not define, and which are
# therefore NOT conformance: a pass or a fail would measure Dommy against a
# prototype rather than a standard. They are not vendored, and
# script/refresh-corpus.rb refuses to run while one is present. One path per
# line, relative to wpt/corpus.
#
# urlpattern/urlpattern-compare.tentative.any.js: tests
#   URLPattern.compareComponent, which is not part of the URL Pattern Standard
#   (it was a Chromium prototype; workerd skips it with the same reason). Its
#   helper resources/urlpattern-compare-tests.tentative.js and its
#   resources/urlpattern-compare-test-data.json came with it and are gone too.
#
# urlpattern/urlpattern-generate.tentative.any.js: tests URLPattern.generate,
#   likewise absent from the URL Pattern Standard. Its
#   resources/urlpattern-generate-test-data.json came with it and is gone too.
#
# shadow-dom/declarative/tentative/shadowrootadoptedstylesheets/*: the
#   declarative shadowrootadoptedstylesheets attribute, a proposal (whatwg/html#12339) that is not in the HTML Standard
#   and not in its fragment serialization algorithm. The directory, support/
#   included, is not vendored.
#
# html/interaction/focus/focusgroup/*: the focusgroup attribute, an Open UI proposal
#   (https://open-ui.org/components/focusgroup.explainer/) that is not in the
#   HTML Standard; every test of it is tentative. The directory, resources/
#   included, is not vendored.
